  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem ehealth-usage-context-type</b></p><a name=\"ehealth-usage-context-type\"> </a><a name=\"hcehealth-usage-context-type\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://ehealth.sundhed.dk/cs/ehealth-usage-context-type</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td><td><b>Dansk (Danish, da)</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">activity<a name=\"ehealth-usage-context-type-activity\"> </a></td><td>activity type</td><td>The type of activity in which it is relevant to use a module/element having this use context (see http://hl7.org/fhir/metadatatypes.html#UsageContext). For this context type, the value should be a code taken from the http://ehealth.sundhed.dk/vs/activitydefinition-code value set</td><td>Type af aktivitet i hvilken det er relevant at benytte det modul/element/ressource, der har nærværende brugskontekst (UsageContext).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">supports<a name=\"ehealth-usage-context-type-supports\"> </a></td><td>supports</td><td>The type of activity supported by a module/element having this use context (see http://hl7.org/fhir/metadatatypes.html#UsageContext). For this context type, the value should be a code taken from the http://ehealth.sundhed.dk/vs/activitydefinition-code value set</td><td>Type af aktivitet understøttet af det modul/element/ressource, der har nærværende brugskontekst (UsageContext).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">range<a name=\"ehealth-usage-context-type-range\"> </a></td><td>range</td><td>The type of reference range with which it is relevant to use a module/element having this use context (see http://hl7.org/fhir/metadatatypes.html#UsageContext). For this context type, the value should be a code taken from the http://ehealth.sundhed.dk/vs/reference-range-type value set</td><td>Type af grænseværdi med hvilken det er relevant at benytte det modul/element/ressource, der har nærværende brugskontekst (UsageContext).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">questionnaire-related<a name=\"ehealth-usage-context-type-questionnaire-related\"> </a></td><td>questionnaire related</td><td>The type of questionnaire element with which it is relevant to use a coded values/id registries having this use context (see http://hl7.org/fhir/metadatatypes.html#UsageContext). For this context type, the value should be a code taken from the http://ehealth.sundhed.dk/vs/questionnaire-elements value set</td><td>Type af spørgeskemaelement med hvilken det er relevant at benytte kodede værdier/id register, der har nærværende brugskontekst (UsageContext).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">system-treatment-area<a name=\"ehealth-usage-context-type-system-treatment-area\"> </a></td><td>system treatment area</td><td>The coexistence-tag for which the treatment area collection ValueSet is relevant. For this context type, the value should be a code taken from the http://ehealth.sundhed.dk/vs/ehealth-system value set</td><td>Markering af hvilket sameksistens-tag den pågældende samling af behandlingsområder er tilknyttet.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">condition-qualification<a name=\"ehealth-usage-context-type-condition-qualification\"> </a></td><td>condition qualification</td><td>Qualification of condition. For this context type, the value shall be a code from http://ehealth.sundhed.dk/vs/condition-qualification</td><td>Kvalificering af diagnose</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">body-site<a name=\"ehealth-usage-context-type-body-site\"> </a></td><td>body site</td><td>Placement on the body. For this context type, the value shall be a code from http://ehealth.sundhed.dk/vs/usage-context-body-site</td><td>Placering på kroppen</td></tr></table></div>"
  ] ;
